{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Those who remained.</b> Of the death — this teaches that even upon them a death-punishment was incurred for the sin of the calf. For so it is stated (Deuteronomy 9): ״וּבְאַהֲרֹן הִתְאַנַּף ה׳ מְאֹד לְהַשְׁמִידוֹ״, and הַשְׁמָדָה is nothing but the annihilation of children, as it is stated (Amos 2): ״וָאַשְׁמִיד פִּרְיוֹ מִמַּעַל״, and the prayer of Moses annulled half of it, as it is stated (Deuteronomy 9): ״וָאֶתְפַּלֵּל גַּם בְּעַד אַהֲרֹן בָּעֵת הַהִיא״." "<b>Take the meal-offering.</b> Even though you are אוֹנְנִים, and consecrated offerings are forbidden to an אוֹנֵן." "<b>The meal-offering.</b> This is the meal-offering of the eighth day and the meal-offering of Nahshon (Sifra)." "<b>And you shall eat it unleavened.</b> What is the verse saying? Since it is a communal meal-offering and a one-time meal-offering, and there is nothing like it for the generations, Scripture needed to specify in it the law of other meal-offerings (ibid.)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:43.950669915Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}